<title>USA: Kingdom of Thailand to tap U.S. corp debt market.</title>
<headline>Kingdom of Thailand to tap U.S. corp debt market.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kingdom of Thailand is expected to tap the corporate bond primary market with a $700 million two-part debt offering in early April, syndicate sources said.</p>
<p>The A2/A rated deal is expected to include a $500 million 10-year issue and a $200 million 30-year tranche, sources said.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to be underwritten by joint managers Lehman Brothers and Salomon Brothers Inc, they added.</p>
<p>(( --Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
